  "data": {
    "body": "Consider the linear system x'=Ax, where A = $\\begin{bmatrix}\n-5 & 1 \\\\\n4 & -2\n\\end{bmatrix}$\\[\\](a) Find two linearly independent solutions of the system.\\[\\](b) Use the solutions found in part (a) to calculate the exponential matrix $e^{At}$.",
    "solution": "\\[\n\\text{a)  } x_1(t)=e^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{bmatrix}, \\: x_2(t)=e^{-6t}\\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix} \\\\[10pt]\n\n\\text{b)  } \\begin{bmatrix}\n\\frac{e^{-t} + 4e^{-6t}}{5} & \\frac{e^{-t} - e^{-6t}}{5} \\\\\n\\frac{4e^{-t} - 4e^{-6t}}{5} & \\frac{4e^{-t} + e^{-6t}}{5}\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\]",
    "answerChoices": []
  },
